  {
    "lesson_id": "038",
    "trigger_word": "electricity",
    "trigger_card_number": 619,
    "title": "LESSON 38: SCIENCE BUILDS",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "ELECTRON (ἤλεκτρον) is amber, and THERM",
          "(θέρμη) is heat.",
          "",
          "  electrode     amber + path",
          "  electrolyte   amber + loosened",
          "  thermostat    heat + standing",
          "  hyperthermia  over + heat",
          "",
          "Rubbed amber picks up straw. That parlour",
          "trick gave the whole science its name.",
          "",
          "From here on, many words were not worn",
          "smooth by centuries. They were built on",
          "purpose, in one sitting, by someone naming",
          "a new thing, and Greek was the quarry the",
          "parts came from.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 15 CARDS: amber and heat."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 38"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "039",
