    "trigger_card_number": 634,
    "title": "LESSON 39: WATER, FIRE, AIR",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "HYDRO (ὕδωρ) is water, PYR (πῦρ) is fire,",
          "and AERO (ἀήρ) is air.",
          "",
          "  hydraulic     water + pipe",
          "  pyrolysis     fire + loosening",
          "  aerobic       air + life",
          "  anaerobic     without + air + life",
          "",
          "Hydrogen is the water-maker. It was named",
          "for what it leaves behind when it burns.",
          "",
          "Pyrite throws sparks off steel, which is",
          "why it is the firestone, and fool's gold",
          "only to the disappointed.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 17 CARDS: water, fire and air."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 39"
      }
    ]
  },
