    "title": "LESSON 40: COLOR, SHARP, STONE",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "CHROMA (χρῶμα) is colour, OXY (ὀξύς) is",
          "sharp, and LITH (λίθος) is stone.",
          "",
          "  monochrome    one + colour",
          "  oxymoron      sharp + dull",
          "  megalith      great + stone",
          "  lithograph    stone + drawing",
          "",
          "Chromosomes are coloured bodies. They took",
          "the dye readily under the first good",
          "microscopes, and the name stuck.",
          "",
          "Oxygen is a mistake left standing.",
          "Lavoisier named it the acid-maker, sure",
          "that every acid held it. Many do not.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 16 CARDS: colour, acid and stone."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 40"
      }
    ]
