    "trigger_card_number": 680,
    "title": "LESSON 42: NATURE, ANIMAL, PLANT",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "PHYSIS (φύσις) is nature, ZOON (ζῷον) an",
          "animal, and PHYTON (φυτόν) a plant.",
          "",
          "  physiology    nature + study",
          "  zooplankton   animal + drifting",
          "  phytoplankton plant + drifting",
          "  neophyte      new + planted",
          "",
          "The sea's drift is halved by two of these",
          "roots: the plants that make the food and",
          "the animals that eat them.",
          "",
          "Metaphysics is named for a shelf. The book",
          "sat after the Physics in Aristotle, and",
          "meta means after.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 16 CARDS: nature and life."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 42"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "043",
    "trigger_word": "nitrogen",
    "trigger_card_number": 696,
    "title": "LESSON 43: BIRTH, WOMAN, MAN",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "GENOS (γένος) is birth or kind, GYNE",
          "(γυνή) is woman, and ANER (ἀνήρ) is man.",
          "",
          "  genealogy     descent + study",
          "  misogyny      hatred + woman",
          "  polyandry     many + man",
          "  android       man + resembling",
          "",
          "The ending -gen means producing. Nitrogen",
          "produces nitre, hydrogen produces water,",
          "an androgen produces the male traits.",
          "",
          "Gyne and aner are the woman and the man",
          "themselves. Anthropos, from an earlier",
          "cluster, is the human being either way.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 16 CARDS: birth, woman and man."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 43"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "044",
    "trigger_word": "cytology",
    "trigger_card_number": 712,
    "title": "LESSON 44: CELL, THREAD, KERNEL",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "KYTOS (κύτος) is a cell or hollow, MITOS",
          "(μίτος) a thread, and KARYON (κάρυον) a",
          "nut or kernel.",
          "",
          "  cytoplasm     cell + moulded stuff",
          "  leukocyte     white + cell",
          "  mitosis       thread + process",
          "  eukaryote     true + kernel",
          "",
          "The thread and the kernel are what the",
          "first microscopes showed: chromosomes",
          "drawn out like fibres, and a nucleus in",
          "the cell like a nut in its shell.",
          "",
          "A prokaryote is the cell that came before",
          "the kernel. Bacteria keep no nucleus.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 13 CARDS: cells and kernels."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 44"
      }
    ]
  },
