  {
    "lesson_id": "046",
    "trigger_word": "humanoid",
    "trigger_card_number": 743,
    "title": "LESSON 46: LIKE, STATE, LOOSEN",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "OID (-οειδής) means resembling, OSIS",
          "(-ωσις) names a condition, and LYSIS",
          "(λύσις) is a loosening.",
          "",
          "  spheroid      resembling a sphere",
          "  sclerosis     hard + condition",
          "  dialysis      through + loosening",
          "  paralysis     beside + loosening",
          "",
          "These are endings, not roots. They say",
          "what kind of thing the word is before you",
          "know its subject.",
          "",
          "Oid warns you not to trust what stands",
          "before it: a factoid only resembles a",
          "fact, which is what Mailer coined it for.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 19 CARDS: three endings."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 46"
      }
    ]
